2026-04-02 Update - Monthly Vulnerability Audit:
- Monthly audit was due because no audit entry existed in `progress.ai` within the last 30 days.
- Confirmed there is no `frontend/` Node workspace in this repository, so the audit scope for this repo is Java/backend only.
- Initial audit command:
- `mvn org.owasp:dependency-check-maven:check -DnvdApiKey=***`
- Initial findings from OWASP Dependency-Check:
- `spring-core-6.1.13` flagged for `CVE-2024-38820`
- `tomcat-embed-core-10.1.30` flagged for multiple CVEs including `CVE-2024-50379`, `CVE-2024-56337`, `CVE-2025-24813`, and `CVE-2026-24734`
- `log4j-api-2.23.1` flagged for `CVE-2025-68161`
- Remediation applied in `pom.xml`:
- Upgraded the Spring Boot parent from `3.3.4` to `3.5.9`
- Added explicit managed-property overrides:
- `tomcat.version=10.1.52`
- `log4j2.version=2.25.3`
- Validation commands after remediation:
- `mvn test -q`
- `mvn org.owasp:dependency-check-maven:check -DnvdApiKey=***`
- Validation results:
- Test suite exited successfully after the dependency updates.
- Follow-up OWASP Dependency-Check completed with no reported vulnerable dependencies.
- Generated report path: `target/dependency-check-report.html`
- Audit caveats noted during the run:
- Dependency-Check emitted a non-fatal warning that the `.NET Assembly Analyzer` could not initialize because `dotnet` is not installed; the Java audit still completed successfully.
- OSS Index analysis was skipped because authenticated Sonatype OSS Index credentials were not configured.
- Spec Kit task note: the monthly vulnerability audit task can be considered complete for `2026-04-02`.

