2026-04-02 Update - `001-security-hardening` Implementation:
- Created the dedicated feature branch `feature/001-security-hardening` from `main`.
- Updated `src/main/resources/application.properties` to remove committed plaintext datasource values and replace them with environment-backed properties:
- `SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL`
- `SPRING_DATASOURCE_USERNAME`
- `SPRING_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD`
- Added inline comments in `src/main/resources/application.properties` documenting those required env vars in a safe repo-visible location.
- Removed the datasource password startup print from `src/main/java/com/fishdan/myorgchart/MyOrgChartApplication.java`.
- Added a `PasswordEncoder` bean in `src/main/java/com/fishdan/myorgchart/MyOrgChartApplication.java`.
- Updated `src/main/java/com/fishdan/myorgchart/organization/OrganizationService.java` so `createOrganization` hashes the submitted password before saving.
- Updated `src/main/java/com/fishdan/myorgchart/organization/Organization.java` to make the password field write-only for JSON serialization so password hashes are not returned in API responses.
- Added `spring-security-crypto` in `pom.xml` for BCrypt password hashing without pulling in full Spring Security web auth.
- Added automated coverage:
- `src/test/java/com/fishdan/myorgchart/organization/OrganizationServiceTest.java`
- `src/test/java/com/fishdan/myorgchart/organization/OrganizationControllerTest.java`
- Validation:
- `mvn test -q` passed on `feature/001-security-hardening`
- Manual startup verification:
- First `mvn spring-boot:run` attempt with env-provided datasource values proved the app no longer printed the removed password line, but failed because local port `8080` was already in use.
- Re-ran with `mvn spring-boot:run -Dspring-boot.run.arguments=--server.port=0` and the app started successfully against the externalized datasource configuration, then shut down cleanly under `timeout`.
- Manual verification result: externalized datasource configuration works and the previous startup secret leak is gone.
- Spec Kit task note: `T0101`, `T0110`, `T0111`, `T0112`, `T0120`, `T0121`, `T0122`, `T0123`, `T0130`, `T0131`, `T0132`, `T0140`, `T0141`, and `T0142` are complete.
